 I  visited Thames Valley police to observe  firearms training  and in March 2020 the government gave  more than 6 million pounds to forces to  purchase over 7 000 devices increasing  the number of officers who are trained  in and have a taser  in August 2020 we approved the use of  the taser 7 a more accurate and  effective device for policing and in  March we approved the use of taser by  specially trained special constables  I'm committed to ensuring that you have  access to tasers wherever appropriate  of course it's not just violent  criminals on our streets that we are  determined to stop  I also want to see more fraudsters  caught and brought to Justice  and I'm sure that's an ambition that we  all share here  that's why the government is allocating  a further 400 million pounds over the  next three years for tackling economic  crime including fraud  by March 2025 over 330 new officers  dedicated to this work will have been  recruited into the city of London Police  the regional organized crime units and  the National Crime agency  we will replace the current action fraud  system with a new and improved service  and we will increase intelligence  capabilities at the NCA and the National  Security Community to identify and  disrupt the most harmful criminals and  serious organized criminal gangs  and we are making sure that the biggest  technology companies are doing  everything they can to prevent online  fraud through our world-leading Online  safety bill

